From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IORA Build System <build@iora.local>
Date: Sat, 3 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GCC 15 compatibility: add missing <cstdint> includes

GCC 15 no longer implicitly includes <cstdint> through other standard
library headers (specifically <memory>). This causes build failures in
CMake's bundled cppdap library which uses uint32_t without explicitly
including <cstdint>.

Fix by adding the missing #include <cstdint> to both network.h (header)
and socket.h (internal header), which both use uint32_t in their public
API.

Error fixed:
  Utilities/cmcppdap/include/dap/network.h:31:39: error: 'uint32_t' has
  not been declared

References:
  https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-15/porting_to.html
  (headers used less widely: <cstdint> for std::int32_t etc.)

--- a/Utilities/cmcppdap/include/dap/network.h
+++ b/Utilities/cmcppdap/include/dap/network.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #ifndef dap_network_h
 #define dap_network_h
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <functional>
 #include <memory>
 
--- a/Utilities/cmcppdap/src/socket.h
+++ b/Utilities/cmcppdap/src/socket.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 #include "dap/io.h"
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <atomic>
 #include <memory>
